# Packages omitted from omarchy-base.packages on aarch64.
#
# Every entry here is a package with no build path we are willing to take, not merely
# one that is absent from Arch Linux ARM. 122 of the manifest's 148 packages install
# straight from ALARM, and 20 more build from omarchy-pkgs, which already declares
# aarch64 for them. See docs/survey.md in the port repo for the per-package evidence.

# Nowhere: not in ALARM, not in [omarchy], and nothing in the AUR provides it.
# The only genuine casualty in the manifest.
qemu-user-static-binfmt

# No PKGBUILD in omarchy-pkgs. AUR forks (obs-studio-browser, obs-studio-rc) do declare
# aarch64, but running a fork of OBS is not a trade we want. gpu-screen-recorder is
# already in the manifest and resolves for aarch64.
obs-studio

# No PKGBUILD in omarchy-pkgs, and its only reference anywhere in the tree is this
# manifest - it is here for pinta, which is also excluded below.
dotnet-runtime

# No PKGBUILD in omarchy-pkgs. bin/omarchy-theme-set-obsidian exits 0 when the current
# theme ships no obsidian.css, so nothing breaks by its absence. AUR obsidian-bin
# declares aarch64 if it is ever wanted back.
obsidian

# In the [omarchy] database but with no PKGBUILD in omarchy-pkgs, so there is nothing to
# build from. Referenced only by bin/omarchy-install-preinstalls, which is opt-in.
pinta

# Apple Studio Display brightness control. omarchy-pkgs declares arch=('x86_64'
# 'aarch64'), so this one builds fine - it is simply meaningless on this board.
asdcontrol

# Its systemd unit deletes every /usr/lib/modules/* directory that is neither the running
# kernel nor pacman-owned. This board's kernel modules are restored from a tarball and
# owned by nothing, so they match that description exactly -- they survive only while
# `uname -r` happens to equal the directory name. One mismatched boot and the modules that
# make this hardware work are gone: no panthor, no ethernet.
#
# Its purpose -- keeping a running system usable across a pacman kernel upgrade -- cannot
# apply here, because pacman does not manage this kernel (see docs/verification/P1.md).
kernel-modules-hook
